{"number": 24, "text": "                    vx\n                    Mata that thaca      rallacata with havea rathar than anu athar   fa A not ar malo\\\n\n\n                                                 Mr Grey had an accident last night but he’s OK now.\n                     have an accident\n                                                 We had an argument / a row about how to fix the car.\n                     have an argument / a row\n                                                 Let’s have a break when you finish this exercise.\n                     have a break\n\n                                                 | hope we'll have time to have a chat after the meeting.\n                     have a conversation/chat\n                     have difficulty\n                                                 The class had difficulty understanding what to do.\n                     have a dream/nightmare\n                                                 | had a nightmare last night.\n                                                 | had a frightening experience the other day.\n                     have an experience\n                                                 | have a feeling that something is wrong.\n                     have a feeling\n                     have fun / a good time\n                                                    sure you'll have fun on the school trip.\n                                                 The manager wanted to have a look at what we were doing.\n                     have a look\n                                                 Let’s have a party at the end of term.\n                     have a party\n                     have a problem / problems\n                                                 Ask the teacher if you have problems with the exercise.\n                     have a try/go\n                                                 I’tl explain what to do and then you can have a go/try.\n\n\n                                                                                            Reply      Forward\n\n                                   Hi, Jean,\n                                   We're so glad we decided to take a holiday here. Yesterday we took a trip to\n                                   the mountains. First we took a train to a little town and then we took a bus\n                                   going to various villages and got off when we saw one that we took a liking\n                                   to. Of course, we were taking a risk as we didn’t know exactly what we’d find\n                                   there. But we were lucky. Some kids took an interest in us and showed us\n                                   some  great places. We took a lot of photos.\n                                   Have you  done anything  yet about your job? I’d take a chance and leave if I\n                                   were you. No  point in staying somewhere where  the boss has taken a dislike\n                                   to you! Take advantage of being in London  — there are always plenty of jobs\n                                   there.      soon  find something else, so take action, that’s my advice! Good\n                                   luck!\n\n                                   Ellen\n\n\n                                                 You must pay attention to the teacher.\n                     pay attention\n                     pay a compliment\n                                                 | was trying to pay her a compliment but she misunderstood.\n                     pay your (last) respects\n                                                 At a funeral people pay their last respects to the person who has died.\n                     pay tribute [formal]\n                                                 When  Jack retired, his boss made a speech paying tribute to all he had\n                                                 done for the company.\n